1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:01,567
Before a buyer

2
00:00:01,567 --> 00:00:03,533
pays for your biomass,

3
00:00:03,533 --> 00:00:05,533
they check five things.

4
00:00:05,533 --> 00:00:08,233
Know them before you quote.

5
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:09,133
One.

6
00:00:09,133 --> 00:00:10,067
Moisture.

7
00:00:10,067 --> 00:00:12,400
Wet fuel burns poorly,

8
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:15,900
and you end up transporting water.

9
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:18,967
Most buyers set a maximum.

10
00:00:19,333 --> 00:00:19,767
Two.

11
00:00:19,767 --> 00:00:20,367
GCV.

12
00:00:20,367 --> 00:00:22,033
The heat your fuel

13
00:00:22,033 --> 00:00:23,433
gives per kilo.

14
00:00:23,433 --> 00:00:25,033
Below the minimum,

15
00:00:25,033 --> 00:00:27,300
the load can be rejected,

16
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:29,233
or the price cut.

17
00:00:29,733 --> 00:00:30,333
Three.

18
00:00:30,333 --> 00:00:30,767
Ash.

19
00:00:30,767 --> 00:00:33,333
More ash means more cleaning,

20
00:00:33,333 --> 00:00:36,200
and more wear on the boiler.

21
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,133
Four.

22
00:00:37,133 --> 00:00:37,667
Size.

23
00:00:37,667 --> 00:00:40,600
Pellets and briquettes must match

24
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:42,500
the size the buyer's

25
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,700
feeding system takes.

26
00:00:45,133 --> 00:00:45,600
Five.

27
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:46,500
Consistency.

28
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:48,833
One good sample is not enough.

29
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:50,067
Every truck has

30
00:00:50,067 --> 00:00:51,867
to match the spec.

31
00:00:51,967 --> 00:00:53,600
Get these five right,

32
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:54,800
and price talks

33
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:56,533
get a lot easier.

34
00:00:56,767 --> 00:00:59,900
Screenshot this before your next quote.

